  },
  {
   "n": 1,
   "id": "9f8423e",
   "doc": "wp-post#168788",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 1,
     "text": "Cannabis Seeds vs Clones: Understanding the Foundation of Cannabis Cultivation",
     "demote": true
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Cannabis starts long before flower reaches dispensary shelves. Every plant begins its journey from either a <a href=\"/categories/seeds/\"><strong>seed</strong></a> or a <a href=\"/categories/clones/\" data-link=\"dead\"><strong>clone</strong></a>, and understanding the difference between the two is one of the best ways to learn how cannabis is grown, selected, and cultivated.</p><p>At <strong>Cape Cod Cannabis</strong>, we believe education helps customers feel more connected to the products they enjoy. Whether you are curious about cultivation, interested in cannabis genetics, or simply want to understand where your flower comes from, this guide breaks down the basics of cannabis seeds and clones in a simple, approachable way.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "image",
     "ref": "assets/source/9375c58c-2c.png",
     "srcUrl": "https://b2702268.assetcdn.net/2.0/2702268/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2c.png?lossy=2&strip=0&webp=1",
     "alt": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "titleAttr": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "w": 43,
     "h": 38,
     "inHeading": true
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "What Are Cannabis Seeds?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Cannabis seeds are the starting point of a new cannabis plant. Just like seeds from fruits or vegetables, cannabis seeds contain the genetic blueprint that determines how the plant will grow.</p><p>Each seed has the potential to develop unique traits, including:</p><ul><li>Aroma and flavor</li><li>Cannabinoid levels like THC and CBD</li><li>Plant size and structure</li><li>Flowering time</li><li>Terpene profile</li><li>Resistance to pests and environmental stress</li></ul><p>Seeds are created through pollination and are commonly used by breeders and cultivators to develop new strains and preserve cannabis genetics.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "image",
     "ref": "assets/source/9375c58c-2c.png",
     "srcUrl": "https://b2702268.assetcdn.net/2.0/2702268/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2c.png?lossy=2&strip=0&webp=1",
     "alt": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "titleAttr": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "w": 43,
     "h": 38,
     "inHeading": true
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "Types of Cannabis Seeds"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>There are several different types of cannabis seeds commonly used in cultivation.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Regular Seeds"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Regular seeds can grow into either male or female plants. Growers using regular seeds often select the strongest female plants for flower production.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Feminized Seeds"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Feminized seeds are bred specifically to produce female plants, which are the plants that grow cannabinoid rich flower. These are extremely popular because they reduce uncertainty during cultivation.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Autoflower Seeds"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Autoflower seeds begin flowering automatically based on age rather than light cycles. They are often chosen for faster grow times and simplicity.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "image",
     "ref": "assets/source/9375c58c-2c.png",
     "srcUrl": "https://b2702268.assetcdn.net/2.0/2702268/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2c.png?lossy=2&strip=0&webp=1",
     "alt": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "titleAttr": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "w": 43,
     "h": 38,
     "inHeading": true
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "Benefits of Growing from Seeds"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Growing cannabis from seeds offers several advantages.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Genetic Diversity"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Each seed produces a unique plant, even within the same strain family. This diversity allows breeders to discover new combinations of flavor, potency, and growth traits.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Strong Root Development"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Seed grown plants often develop deep taproots, helping create strong and resilient growth.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Long Term Preservation"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Seeds can be stored for extended periods, making them valuable for preserving cannabis genetics over time.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "New Strain Creation"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Most new cannabis strains begin through seed breeding programs that combine genetics from multiple plants.</p>"
    }
   ]
  },
