  {
   "n": 4,
   "id": "8c20e2b",
   "doc": "wp-post#168788",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "image",
     "ref": "assets/source/9375c58c-2c.png",
     "srcUrl": "https://b2702268.assetcdn.net/2.0/2702268/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2c.png?lossy=2&strip=0&webp=1",
     "alt": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "titleAttr": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "w": 43,
     "h": 38,
     "inHeading": true
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "What Are Cannabis Clones?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>A cannabis clone is a cutting taken from a mature “mother plant.” The cutting is rooted and grown into a new plant that is genetically identical to the original.</p><p>In simple terms:<br>A clone is essentially a copy of another cannabis plant.</p><p>Clones allow growers to reproduce plants with consistent characteristics, ensuring predictable results from harvest to harvest.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "image",
     "ref": "assets/source/9375c58c-2c.png",
     "srcUrl": "https://b2702268.assetcdn.net/2.0/2702268/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2c.png?lossy=2&strip=0&webp=1",
     "alt": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "titleAttr": "Cape Cod Cannabis Recreational Dispensary in Wellfleet, MA",
     "w": 43,
     "h": 38,
     "inHeading": true
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 2,
     "text": "Benefits of Cannabis Clones"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Clones are widely used throughout the cannabis industry for consistency and efficiency.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Genetic Consistency"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Since clones are exact copies of the mother plant, growers know exactly what traits to expect.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Faster Growth Cycle"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Clones skip the germination stage, which can shorten cultivation time.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Reliable Flower Production"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Cultivators often choose clones when they want stable yields and predictable cannabinoid levels.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Preserving Elite Genetics"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>If a grower discovers a particularly exceptional plant, cloning allows those genetics to continue indefinitely.</p>"
    }
   ]
  },
